"""AQS-BLD-018 enclosure, floor plates, stairs and egress (X-BLD-05, A-M-213). Occupant load per level by IBC 1004.5 function factors;
two exits per level (IBC 1006.3.3); stair width = max(1,118 mm, 7.6 mm per occupant) (IBC 1005.3.1, 1011.2); travel distance to an exit
stair from the farthest plate corner against 76 m (F-1, sprinklered, IBC 1017.2). Stairs and the levels they serve come from
models/freecad/building_stack.py geometry (params.py datums). Enclosure UA from IECC 2021 C402 opaque U-factors; design heat loss at the
AQS-SITE-002 99.6 % heating dry bulb. Floor plates from AQS-BLD-016. Run after _frame_check.py."""
import json, math, os, sys
R = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))); os.chdir(R); sys.path.insert(0, R); sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(R, 'models/freecad'))
from flow_graph.param.refs import cite
for k in ('IBC2027_CH10', 'IECC2021_C402', 'NFPA101_2027'): cite(k)
import params as P
Lp, Wp = P.PLATE_L, P.PLATE_W; A = Lp*Wp/1e6; z0r = P.HYDRO_RES_Z0; clr = P.HYDRO_RES_CLEAR
LV = [('L-2', P.Z_Lm2, 'lower reservoir and catch (maintenance only)', 27.9, 0.15), ('L-1', P.Z_Lm1, 'process (industrial)', 9.3, 1.0),
      ('L0', P.Z_L0, 'process and shop (industrial)', 9.3, 1.0), ('L1', P.Z_L1, 'habitation (residential) + farm (agricultural storage)', (18.6 + 27.9)/2, 1.0),
      ('L2', P.Z_L2, 'farm and roof tank (storage)', 27.9, 1.0)] + [(f'R{i+1}', z0r + i*clr, 'upper reservoir (maintenance walkway only)', 27.9, 0.15) for i in range(P.HYDRO_RES_LEVELS)] + [('ROOF', P.Z_ROOF, 'roof PV (maintenance)', 27.9, 1.0)]
z_top = max(P.Z_L2 + 2000, P.Z_ROOF + 2000)
ST = [('STAIR_P', P.Z_L0, z_top, P.STAIR_BOX), ('STAIR_S1', P.Z_L0, max(P.Z_L2, P.Z_ROOF), P.STAIR_BOX), ('STAIR_S2', P.Z_L0, P.Z_L2, P.STAIR_BOX),
      ('STAIR_MAINT', P.Z_Lm2, P.Z_L0 + 500, P.STAIR_MAINT_W), ('STAIR_SERVICE', P.Z_Lm2, P.Z_L0, min(P.STAIR_SERVICE_L, P.STAIR_SERVICE_W))]
POS = {'STAIR_P': (P.CORE_X + 1300, P.CORE_Y + 2400), 'STAIR_S1': (1500, Wp - 1500), 'STAIR_S2': (Lp - 1500, 1500), 'STAIR_MAINT': (P.CORE_X + 3450, P.CORE_Y + 4600), 'STAIR_SERVICE': (P.STAIR_SERVICE_X + 1200, P.STAIR_SERVICE_Y + 1800)}
rows = []; bad = 0
for lv, z, use, f, frac in LV:
    occ = math.ceil(A*frac/f); s = [n for n, a, b, w in ST if a <= z <= b]; need_w = max(1118, 7.6*occ)
    cl = min(((w - 300)/2 if w >= 2400 else w - 150) for n, a, b, w in ST if n in s) if s else 0      # clear width per flight
    corners = [(0, 0), (Lp, 0), (0, Wp), (Lp, Wp)]
    td = max(min(abs(cx - POS[n][0]) + abs(cy - POS[n][1]) for n in s) for cx, cy in corners)/1000 if s else float('inf')
    ok = len(s) >= 2 and cl >= need_w and td <= 76; bad += not ok
    rows.append((lv, z/1000, use, occ, ', '.join(s) or '-', len(s), need_w, cl, td, 'pass' if ok else 'FAIL'))
H_above = P.Z_ROOF/1000; per = 2*(Lp + Wp)/1000; Uw, Ur = 0.534, 0.199; dT = 21 - (-7.2)
UA = Uw*per*H_above + Ur*A; Q = UA*dT/1000
md = ['# Enclosure, floor plates, stairs and egress', '', 'Document number: AQS-BLD-018', 'Revision: B', 'Date: 2026-10-25',
      'Authority: AQS-PLAN-007 task X-BLD-05; method of AQS-EGR-001; assumption A-M-213. Generated by `docs-authority/_egress_env.py`; do not edit this page by hand. Study; this page is not stamped by a Professional Engineer (PE).', '',
      '| Rev | Description | Date |', '|---|---|---|', '| A | First issue | 2026-10-16 |',
      '| B | Purpose and scope added; text rewritten to the documentation style guide (AQS-DOC-002). No level, stair or value changed. | 2026-10-25 |', '',
      '## 1. Purpose and scope', '',
      'This page checks that every level of the plant building can be evacuated, and states the construction of the floors and of the outer '
      'envelope. Egress is the route by which occupants leave a building in an emergency. For each level the check counts the occupants, '
      'the stairs that serve the level, the stair width needed and provided, and the longest travel distance to a stair. It then gives the '
      'floor plate construction and the heat loss through the envelope.', '',
      '## 2. Egress from each level', '',
      'A level passes if it is served by at least two stairs, if the clear width of every flight is at least the width needed, and if the '
      'travel distance from the farthest corner of the plate to the nearest stair is no more than 76 m. The width needed is the larger of '
      '1118 mm and 7.6 mm for each occupant. Table 2.1 gives the result for each level; z is the floor elevation.', '',
      'Table 2.1. Egress by level', '',
      '| Level | z m | Use | Occupants | Stairs serving | Exits | Stair width needed mm | Clear provided mm | Travel to stair m (limit 76) | Result |', '|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
md += [f'| {a} | {b:.1f} | {c} | {d} | {e} | {f} | {g:.0f} | {h:.0f} | {i:.1f} | {j} |' for a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h, i, j in rows]
md += ['', ('No level fails the check.' if not bad else f'{bad} levels fail the check.'),
 '', 'Two changes were made to the model at revision A to pass the check. First, the stair boxes were widened from 2400 mm to 2600 mm (STAIR_BOX) '
     'and STAIR_MAINT from 1200 mm to 1300 mm, so that each flight has 1150 mm clear; IBC 1011.2 requires 1118 mm, and the old 2400 mm box gave '
     '1100 mm. Second, STAIR_P and STAIR_S1 were extended to the roof (`models/freecad/building_stack.py`). Before this, the stairs stopped 2 m '
     'above L2, and the reservoir levels R1 to R3 and the roof had no stair.',
 '', '## 3. Floor plates', '', f'Every suspended level is a {P.SLAB_THK} mm concrete slab carried on the steel beams of AQS-BLD-016, over the {Lp/1000:.0f} x {Wp/1000:.0f} m plate ({A:.0f} m2). The reservoir floors and walls are water-retaining concrete to ACI 350. Level L-2 bears on the foundation mat of AQS-BLD-017. The floors have a fire-resistance rating of 2 h between levels (AQS-HSE-001) and 3 h between the life-support levels and the process levels.',
 '', '## 4. Enclosure', '', f'Above grade the walls are insulated metal panels with a thermal transmittance (U-value) of {Uw} W/m2K, over a perimeter of {per:.0f} m and a height of {H_above:.1f} m. The roof has an area of {A:.0f} m2 and a U-value of {Ur} W/m2K. Both values meet IECC 2021 section C402 for climate zone 3. The product of U-value and area (UA) for the envelope is {UA:,.0f} W/K, which gives a design heat loss of {Q:.1f} kW at a temperature difference of {dT:.1f} K (the 99.6 % winter design condition of AQS-SITE-002).',
 '', 'Below grade the basement walls are cast concrete, waterproofed and drained to the CATCH_TANK sump (AQS-BLD-017).']
open('docs-authority/ENCLOSURE_EGRESS.md', 'w').write('\n'.join(md) + '\n'); print(bad, [r for r in rows if r[-1] == 'FAIL'])
